1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,006
What if your phone showed tomorrow's photos?

2
00:00:03,046 --> 00:00:05,675
You open the gallery and there's a picture

3
00:00:05,715 --> 00:00:07,072
you haven't taken yet:

4
00:00:07,112 --> 00:00:08,407
you, covered in cake,

5
00:00:08,447 --> 00:00:10,567
standing in a very confused crowd.

6
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:13,139
So you dodge the cake.

7
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:15,931
Next morning, you spot the exact same room,

8
00:00:15,971 --> 00:00:17,749
but now it's perfectly calm.

9
00:00:17,789 --> 00:00:18,918
The photo changed.

10
00:00:18,958 --> 00:00:22,424
Apparently, tomorrow only exists until you look at it.

11
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:25,181
Photos become a habit.

12
00:00:25,221 --> 00:00:26,253
A winning goal.

13
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:27,110
A new puppy.

14
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:29,181
A rainy day with no umbrella.

15
00:00:29,221 --> 00:00:30,753
You carry an umbrella.

16
00:00:30,793 --> 00:00:31,824
You win a goal.

17
00:00:31,864 --> 00:00:33,967
Your friends call you psychic,

18
00:00:34,007 --> 00:00:36,110
and you politely refuse a hat.

19
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:40,022
Then one photo makes your stomach drop.

20
00:00:40,062 --> 00:00:42,098
It's your grandfather's garden,

21
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:44,776
empty, with one chair left in the grass.

22
00:00:44,816 --> 00:00:46,919
You stare at it for a long while

23
00:00:46,959 --> 00:00:49,196
before you realise: you have time.

24
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:52,044
You head to the garden.

25
00:00:52,084 --> 00:00:54,813
He is there, humming over the tomatoes,

26
00:00:54,853 --> 00:00:56,447
and you stay for hours.

27
00:00:56,487 --> 00:00:58,649
The new photo shows two chairs,

28
00:00:58,689 --> 00:01:00,992
two cups, and a very smug tomato.

29
00:01:01,032 --> 00:01:02,910
Some futures can be edited.

30
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:06,855
Scientists would say a phone cannot see the

31
00:01:06,895 --> 00:01:09,746
future, because the future hasn't happened yet.

32
00:01:09,786 --> 00:01:11,406
In this thought experiment,

33
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:13,744
the gallery is less a crystal ball and

34
00:01:13,784 --> 00:01:15,281
more a gentle suggestion.

35
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:17,682
Here is the twist.

36
00:01:17,722 --> 00:01:19,180
One last photo appears:

37
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:21,264
you, today, standing right here,

38
00:01:21,304 --> 00:01:24,390
holding your phone, staring at that exact photo.

39
00:01:24,430 --> 00:01:27,581
You look up, and the camera in the corner blinks.

40
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:30,314
So you pocket the phone,

41
00:01:30,354 --> 00:01:31,504
grin at the camera,

42
00:01:31,544 --> 00:01:33,321
and strike a ridiculous pose.

43
00:01:33,361 --> 00:01:35,389
Tomorrow's photo updates at once:

44
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:37,457
you laughing, sunrise behind you,

45
00:01:37,497 --> 00:01:39,524
with absolutely no cake in sight.
